# 1. Project objective

The goal was to build a simple Node.js application, package it into a Docker image, publish the image to Docker Hub automatically using GitHub Actions, identify builds with unique Git commit SHA tags, and practise retrieving an older image for rollback.

This project demonstrates several important DevOps skills:

- Linux terminal navigation and file management
- Node.js application basics
- Docker image creation and container management
- Git version control
- GitHub repository management
- Docker Hub authentication and image publishing
- GitHub Actions CI/CD automation
- Repository secrets management
- Container troubleshooting
- Image versioning and rollback preparation

## Final architecture

Developer changes code → Git commit → Push to GitHub → GitHub Actions runs → Docker image builds → Image is pushed to Docker Hub → Image can be pulled and run as a container.

